// « Composant » (Features/annotationComponents): ONE drawn polyline, several
// annotations of different templates.
//
//   - a COMPONENT template (`drawingShape: "COMPONENT"`) is drawn like a
//     POLYLINE (line or band) and lists the templates it generates:
//     `componentItems: [{ annotationTemplateId, enabled, type? }]` — templates
//     of the same listing, `enabled` = generated by default, `type` =
//     "POLYLINE" | "STRIP" (default: from the `defaultTool` of the template),
//     `stripOrientation` = side of a STRIP item RELATIVE to the band of the
//     component: 1 (default) = same side, -1 = opposite side;
//   - the drawn annotation (the SOURCE) is a regular POLYLINE / STRIP row of
//     the component template. `componentItemsEnabled: { [templateId]: bool }`
//     overrides the defaults per annotation (drawing helper, edit toolbar);
//     `componentApplied: { signature, count }` is stamped by the sync;
//   - the generated annotations (the CHILDREN) are regular rows tagged
//     `componentSourceAnnotationId` + `componentElementKey` (the id of their
//     template). They SHARE the point refs of the source: moving a vertex of
//     the component moves them all, with nothing to recompute. Their geometry
//     is never edited directly.
//
// Display (applyComponentDisplay): the children stand for the component; the
// source is only drawn once selected, in place of its children.
export const COMPONENT_SHAPE = "COMPONENT";

export const COMPONENT_ITEM_TYPE_POLYLINE = "POLYLINE";
export const COMPONENT_ITEM_TYPE_STRIP = "STRIP";
